1
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:15,749
It's okay.

2
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:18,718
I will settle everything.

3
00:00:20,787 --> 00:00:22,956
Ms. Tabatake! Stop!

4
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:24,190
I love you.

5
00:00:26,292 --> 00:00:27,327
Ms. Tabatake!

6
00:00:52,952 --> 00:00:55,221
Sorry to come so late at night.

7
00:00:55,288 --> 00:00:57,690
There's something I needed
to ask you right away.

8
00:00:59,426 --> 00:01:02,629
May I ask you about your mom?

9
00:01:05,632 --> 00:01:06,533
Uh…

10
00:01:08,034 --> 00:01:13,506
She said she was going to your house
before she left the hospital, right?

11
00:01:14,841 --> 00:01:15,809
Yes.

12
00:01:15,875 --> 00:01:19,245
Did she say anything else?

13
00:01:19,979 --> 00:01:22,649
Why did she want to go home?

14
00:01:26,252 --> 00:01:29,022
Was she different from usual?

15
00:01:34,727 --> 00:01:39,432
Mom said, "Once I'm discharged,
let's have crab pizza."

16
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:41,835
Okay.

17
00:01:43,636 --> 00:01:45,839
What else did she say?

18
00:01:45,905 --> 00:01:48,108
Can you leave her alone for today?

19
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:50,243
I'm begging you.

20
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,782
Why doesn't Mommy answer the phone?

21
00:01:56,916 --> 00:02:00,820
Nono, your aunt
is on her way here from Obihiro.

22
00:02:00,887 --> 00:02:03,156
When she gets here, we'll talk about--

23
00:02:03,223 --> 00:02:06,860
Why not now? Where is Mommy?

24
00:02:10,763 --> 00:02:12,966
Who do you want to hear the answer from?

25
00:02:19,038 --> 00:02:20,773
Dr. Yoshino.

26
00:02:38,791 --> 00:02:42,529
Your mom can't come back.

27
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:48,101
She passed away.

28
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:53,173
She died?

29
00:02:54,407 --> 00:02:55,708
Why?

30
00:02:57,877 --> 00:02:58,878
Uh…

31
00:03:02,148 --> 00:03:03,850
We don't know yet.

32
00:03:05,652 --> 00:03:08,321
Are there things even adults don't know?

33
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:12,091
Yes, many.

34
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:15,061
That's why I want you to tell me
even the smallest details.

35
00:03:15,128 --> 00:03:16,029
Why your mom--

36
00:03:16,095 --> 00:03:18,097
Nono, you did nothing wrong.

37
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:26,139
We doctors, the nurses,
child welfare workers, and the police,

38
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:27,907
we will all help you.

39
00:03:30,176 --> 00:03:31,311
Nono…

40
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:34,214
it's okay.

41
00:03:35,415 --> 00:03:36,916
You're not alone.

42
00:03:44,591 --> 00:03:46,125
Excuse me.

43
00:03:46,192 --> 00:03:47,393
Sorry.

44
00:03:49,028 --> 00:03:50,663
My name is Nao.

45
00:03:51,164 --> 00:03:53,199
Are you a police officer, sir?

46
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:57,704
No. I work in insurance.

47
00:03:59,105 --> 00:04:03,343
When your aunt comes,
please give her this.

48
00:04:03,977 --> 00:04:05,378
I'll help.

49
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:11,951
Excuse us.

50
00:04:15,655 --> 00:04:17,423
-A 24-gauge, please.
-Okay.

51
00:04:18,658 --> 00:04:22,128
If his oxygen level falls below 94,
notify me at once.

52
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:30,970
"It's okay?" Why did I say that to a kid?

53
00:04:32,839 --> 00:04:35,108
There's no way things are okay.

54
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:40,113
Why? Damn it!

55
00:04:57,563 --> 00:05:00,333
Should I take us home?

56
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,001
I'm going back to the station.

57
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,442
They take people to hell.

58
00:05:18,418 --> 00:05:20,153
My apologies!

59
00:05:20,219 --> 00:05:21,487
I'm sorry.

60
00:05:31,464 --> 00:05:32,699
Well?

61
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:37,370
There was no suicide note left
in her home or in her hospital room.

62
00:05:37,937 --> 00:05:39,572
It was probably impulsive.

63
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:42,775
Was it really suicide?

64
00:05:43,376 --> 00:05:46,446
There are several witnesses,
including you.

65
00:05:48,948 --> 00:05:50,683
She was scared.

66
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:55,355
Either Ms. Tabatake
or Ms. Aya is the accomplice.

67
00:05:55,421 --> 00:05:56,856
150 MILLION YEN

68
00:05:58,224 --> 00:06:00,526
We sent her phone to the lab.

69
00:06:00,593 --> 00:06:03,930
Also, this, the bottle analysis.

70
00:06:04,731 --> 00:06:07,767
Only Nikaido's
and Saruwatari's fingerprints.

71
00:06:07,834 --> 00:06:09,435
None were Tabatake's.

72
00:06:09,502 --> 00:06:11,604
I'm glad we got those prints.

73
00:06:11,671 --> 00:06:14,607
We have Tabatake's statement,
only the motive is left.

74
00:06:14,674 --> 00:06:16,442
-Chief.
-What?

75
00:06:16,509 --> 00:06:20,313
You said you would question
Saruwatari again tomorrow. What time?

76
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:22,315
-Why do you want to know?
-I just…

77
00:06:22,382 --> 00:06:25,752
Our goal is to make her tell us
why she gave Nikaido sleeping pills,

78
00:06:26,419 --> 00:06:28,054
that's all, right?

79
00:06:29,522 --> 00:06:30,823
Base to all teams.

80
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:34,694
Due to bad weather,
today's search has been suspended.

81
00:06:34,761 --> 00:06:38,464
We did not find the three missing people
or any belongings.

82
00:06:38,531 --> 00:06:40,233
Tomorrow, after the weather improves,

83
00:06:40,299 --> 00:06:42,935
we'll widen the search
below the north cliff.

84
00:06:43,002 --> 00:06:43,936
That's all.

85
00:06:52,044 --> 00:06:53,112
The sky!

86
00:06:53,179 --> 00:06:55,915
Are you Mr. Nao from
Zennichi Insurance Research?

87
00:06:57,183 --> 00:06:58,518
Who is this?

88
00:06:59,285 --> 00:07:01,554
I'm Chika Kato.

89
00:07:01,621 --> 00:07:04,190
Motoka Tabatake's older sister.

90
00:07:06,993 --> 00:07:08,928
What's your business?

91
00:07:09,829 --> 00:07:11,664
I'm Nao.

92
00:07:12,532 --> 00:07:15,668
Nono gave me this.

93
00:07:15,735 --> 00:07:19,338
I'm handling the insurance investigation
for this case.

94
00:07:20,139 --> 00:07:22,308
It was so sudden.

95
00:07:22,375 --> 00:07:25,178
I didn't know who to talk to
or what to talk about.

96
00:07:26,579 --> 00:07:30,082
My condolences to you for your loss.

97
00:07:32,985 --> 00:07:34,954
Did she have other relatives?

98
00:07:35,021 --> 00:07:38,357
Only me. Our parents have passed.

99
00:07:40,226 --> 00:07:42,361
I'm sorry to ask…

100
00:07:44,197 --> 00:07:48,134
but where will Nono live from now on,
and who will watch over her?

101
00:07:50,269 --> 00:07:55,274
I want to take her,
but my husband is strongly against it.

102
00:07:56,075 --> 00:07:57,944
We have three children of our own.

103
00:08:02,248 --> 00:08:03,349
Um…

104
00:08:04,584 --> 00:08:07,420
I have my sister's life insurance policy.

105
00:08:07,987 --> 00:08:12,492
She told me to handle it if something
happened during her guide work.

106
00:08:12,558 --> 00:08:14,360
Is Nono the beneficiary?

107
00:08:14,427 --> 00:08:15,261
Yes.

108
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:16,596
I'll look at it.

109
00:08:19,765 --> 00:08:21,267
My husband says…

110
00:08:22,134 --> 00:08:25,271
if it's suicide,
the insurance won't be paid.

111
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:26,405
Is that true?

112
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:30,743
Depending on the contract,
it may not be paid.

113
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:34,046
When would it be paid?

114
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:40,186
We have three kids, and my husband said
we can't afford to take care of Nono too.

115
00:08:40,253 --> 00:08:41,087
30 MILLION YEN

116
00:08:42,421 --> 00:08:44,624
It depends on the contract terms.

117
00:08:46,492 --> 00:08:47,527
Okay.

118
00:08:55,167 --> 00:08:57,637
Thank you for the nail clipper.

119
00:08:57,703 --> 00:08:59,005
You got them for me, right?

120
00:08:59,071 --> 00:09:00,139
It was nothing.

121
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,707
-Good morning.
-Hello.

122
00:09:01,774 --> 00:09:03,543
-Good morning.
-Excuse me.

123
00:09:09,148 --> 00:09:11,517
I heard about Ms. Tabatake.

124
00:09:12,251 --> 00:09:14,053
Why did she commit suicide?

125
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:15,988
You said Ms. Tabatake…

126
00:09:17,156 --> 00:09:20,493
gave Mr. Nikaido water, right?

127
00:09:22,528 --> 00:09:26,632
When he said he wanted water…

128
00:09:26,699 --> 00:09:30,269
I have a spare bottle.
Give it to Mr. Nikaido.

129
00:09:31,137 --> 00:09:35,141
Ms. Tabatake told me
to give it to him, so I did.

130
00:09:43,649 --> 00:09:45,518
So you're not all bad.

131
00:09:52,792 --> 00:09:58,264
Why didn't Ms. Tabatake
hand it to him herself?

132
00:09:59,065 --> 00:10:02,401
I've heard Mr. Nikaido was irritable, but…

133
00:10:02,468 --> 00:10:06,505
From the start, she was avoiding him.

134
00:10:06,572 --> 00:10:11,110
Ms. Saruwatari, you've climbed
this mountain several times, right?

135
00:10:11,177 --> 00:10:12,178
Yes.

136
00:10:12,244 --> 00:10:15,681
If someone is falling behind,
can you help?

137
00:10:16,382 --> 00:10:17,917
Yes! Of course.

138
00:10:17,984 --> 00:10:19,585
-Thank you.
-Thanks.

139
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:28,628
Mr. Tsugaru?

140
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:30,963
No.

141
00:10:31,030 --> 00:10:32,198
Tsugaru?

142
00:10:32,765 --> 00:10:36,302
She called him that. I thought
she mistook him for someone else.

143
00:10:36,369 --> 00:10:37,269
Okay.

144
00:10:38,537 --> 00:10:40,940
I heard your daughter is doing better.

145
00:10:42,008 --> 00:10:44,143
You should thank me a little.

146
00:10:48,614 --> 00:10:50,449
Hey, can you take a photo of me?

147
00:10:50,516 --> 00:10:51,684
-Is here okay?
-Yes!

148
00:10:53,686 --> 00:10:57,089
Does that mean the two knew each other?

149
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:58,224
Hello, sir.

150
00:10:58,290 --> 00:10:59,558
-It's possible.
-Hey, let's go!

151
00:11:01,527 --> 00:11:03,129
Excuse me.

152
00:11:03,863 --> 00:11:06,098
I'm Shibasaki from Kitami HQ.

153
00:11:06,599 --> 00:11:10,169
Why did she call Mr. Nikaido "Tsugaru"?

154
00:11:10,236 --> 00:11:12,938
We should investigate
Tabatake and Nikaido's connection.

155
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:13,973
Yes.

156
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,074
Detective!

157
00:11:16,075 --> 00:11:17,176
Yes?

158
00:11:17,243 --> 00:11:18,978
About Ms. Tabatake…

159
00:11:19,545 --> 00:11:22,515
She was talking
with someone on the phone last night.

160
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:26,118
I won't tell the police.

161
00:11:28,988 --> 00:11:33,092
The police believe she felt responsible
for what happened during the tour

162
00:11:33,159 --> 00:11:36,996
and are investigating the possibility
that she drove herself to suicide.

163
00:11:37,063 --> 00:11:40,099
Chief, what the heck
is with today's press conference?

164
00:11:40,166 --> 00:11:42,234
Why did they say she felt responsible?

165
00:11:42,301 --> 00:11:44,236
None of us ever said that.

166
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:46,405
The call records, have they been analyzed?

167
00:11:46,472 --> 00:11:48,240
No unusual calls.

168
00:11:48,808 --> 00:11:53,012
94 percent are calls from family and work,
and the rest are sales calls.

169
00:11:53,846 --> 00:11:55,181
END OF EXTRACTED DATA

170
00:11:55,247 --> 00:11:56,882
This last call

171
00:11:57,550 --> 00:12:00,319
is two minutes and ten seconds long.

172
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:04,724
-Is it really a sales number?
-The lab says it is.

173
00:12:05,257 --> 00:12:07,226
Ms. Tabatake was scared of someone--

174
00:12:07,293 --> 00:12:08,861
Why couldn't you stop her from jumping?!

175
00:12:12,498 --> 00:12:13,799
-Sorry.
-My apologies!

176
00:12:18,671 --> 00:12:22,441
Keep investigating Nikaido
and his connections.

177
00:12:22,508 --> 00:12:23,375
Yes.

178
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,814
Thank you.

179
00:12:31,450 --> 00:12:34,487
Today is Nikaido's funeral.
It's our chance.

180
00:12:34,553 --> 00:12:35,621
Let's do what needs doing.

181
00:12:36,188 --> 00:12:37,656
CALL, 2 MINUTES 10 SECONDS

182
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:44,663
The number you have dialed
is not in service.

183
00:12:45,464 --> 00:12:49,802
Please check and dial again.

184
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:18,430
There aren't many mourners.

185
00:13:18,497 --> 00:13:20,299
Does he not have a lot of friends?

186
00:13:21,033 --> 00:13:22,635
My funeral would be like this.

187
00:13:22,701 --> 00:13:24,637
Don't say that.

188
00:13:29,842 --> 00:13:31,377
That guy again.

189
00:13:31,443 --> 00:13:32,478
Yes.

190
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:36,448
Hello.

191
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:41,453
Here.

192
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,756
I'll give you the receipt later.

193
00:13:46,625 --> 00:13:50,896
Didn't you say
you didn't want to see my face?

194
00:13:50,963 --> 00:13:54,466
I changed my mind.
Sorry for calling you over so suddenly.

195
00:14:02,041 --> 00:14:05,544
Is insurance murder a grave crime?

196
00:14:10,382 --> 00:14:13,185
The motive is vicious, you know.

197
00:14:14,186 --> 00:14:17,323
Even with just one victim,
a death sentence can happen.

198
00:14:17,389 --> 00:14:19,058
You've already decided that

199
00:14:19,892 --> 00:14:23,162
I killed my husband
for the insurance, right?

200
00:14:23,229 --> 00:14:26,265
Finding that out is the police's job.

201
00:14:26,332 --> 00:14:31,570
My job is to gather material to decide
whether the insurance should be paid.

202
00:14:31,637 --> 00:14:34,573
The insurance company decides, not me.

203
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,108
Yes.

204
00:14:36,675 --> 00:14:40,246
The company will decide
based on your investigation?

205
00:14:40,312 --> 00:14:46,352
I believe insurance should be paid justly,
not one yen more or less.

206
00:14:46,418 --> 00:14:48,721
-That's how I investigate--
-What do you want to ask?

207
00:14:53,425 --> 00:14:54,727
Two months ago,

208
00:14:55,261 --> 00:14:59,832
when Mr. Nikaido's insurance
was raised to 150 million yen.

209
00:15:02,001 --> 00:15:04,803
Whose decision was it?

210
00:15:08,307 --> 00:15:09,208
My husband's.

211
00:15:09,875 --> 00:15:11,744
He decided the amount too.

212
00:15:11,810 --> 00:15:14,546
Do you know why he raised it?

213
00:15:16,782 --> 00:15:18,751
It was our tenth wedding anniversary.

214
00:15:21,186 --> 00:15:23,589
When I was 48,

215
00:15:24,723 --> 00:15:28,060
he was only 34, and proposed to me.

216
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:34,366
I thought he would soon switch
to a young girl.

217
00:15:37,202 --> 00:15:39,471
But he stayed my husband for ten years.

218
00:15:41,407 --> 00:15:42,675
So…

219
00:15:44,510 --> 00:15:48,280
instead of promising
to stay with me until death,

220
00:15:50,049 --> 00:15:52,418
he rewrote the contract.

221
00:15:57,189 --> 00:16:00,826
Did you love Mr. Nikaido?

222
00:16:08,067 --> 00:16:09,568
I loved him.

223
00:16:12,905 --> 00:16:17,609
I was physically,
mentally, and financially

224
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:21,080
satisfied with him.

225
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:29,621
I'm lonely without him.

226
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:37,463
Thank you for waiting. Here are his ashes.

227
00:16:50,709 --> 00:16:52,678
I understand.

228
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,082
I know this is a tough time for you,

229
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:01,820
but may I check your financial situation?

230
00:17:03,756 --> 00:17:04,757
Yes.

231
00:17:22,741 --> 00:17:26,512
There's testimony that Teruyuki Nikaido
and Tabatake knew each other.

232
00:17:26,578 --> 00:17:29,615
Tabatake called Nikaido "Tsugaru,"

233
00:17:29,681 --> 00:17:33,018
and Nikaido seemed
to know Tabatake had a daughter.

234
00:17:33,085 --> 00:17:34,820
Whose testimony was that?

235
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:36,021
Saruwatari's.

236
00:17:38,857 --> 00:17:41,293
Didn't this come out in the questioning?

237
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:42,961
-What are you getting at?
-Ogoma!

238
00:17:43,996 --> 00:17:45,731
Don't criticize another squad's work.

239
00:17:46,865 --> 00:17:47,900
My apologies.

240
00:17:49,802 --> 00:17:52,204
We looked into Saruwatari's finances.

241
00:17:53,205 --> 00:17:55,641
She's about four million yen in debt.

242
00:17:58,277 --> 00:17:59,978
About the sleeping pill…

243
00:18:00,045 --> 00:18:05,050
Saruwatari's father, who died last year,
was prescribed Zolpidem for insomnia.

244
00:18:05,651 --> 00:18:07,152
That settles it.

245
00:18:10,856 --> 00:18:13,592
Kitami HQ will be calling the shots.

246
00:18:15,327 --> 00:18:16,795
-That's all.
-Yes, sir!

247
00:18:21,233 --> 00:18:22,801
Ogoma, you…

248
00:18:22,868 --> 00:18:24,036
Officer Ogoma.

249
00:18:24,837 --> 00:18:25,504
Yes?

250
00:18:27,306 --> 00:18:30,175
Won't you help with the investigation?

251
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:33,745
I will!

252
00:18:36,315 --> 00:18:39,451
Oh, my! Did he do it?

253
00:18:39,518 --> 00:18:42,087
You were Saruwatari's student, right?

254
00:18:42,154 --> 00:18:45,390
She was only a temp teacher though.

255
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:47,326
Saruwatari denies the charge.

256
00:18:47,392 --> 00:18:48,527
Hello.

257
00:18:48,594 --> 00:18:49,962
Hello.

258
00:18:50,028 --> 00:18:52,764
We have physical evidence
and Tabatake's testimony.

259
00:18:52,831 --> 00:18:56,735
But the other tour guests are missing.
We can't back up Tabatake's testimony.

260
00:18:57,269 --> 00:19:00,139
It's a hard case,
but for the late Mr. Nikaido,

261
00:19:00,205 --> 00:19:03,075
we want to give it a murder indictment.

262
00:19:05,210 --> 00:19:07,646
So what should I do?

263
00:19:09,748 --> 00:19:11,884
Get a confession from Saruwatari.

264
00:19:13,852 --> 00:19:16,455
Find out what she did
on that mountain and where.

265
00:19:22,794 --> 00:19:25,364
I hear you've asked
to be transferred to another station.

266
00:19:25,430 --> 00:19:26,498
Yes.

267
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:31,870
I've asked many times.

268
00:19:31,937 --> 00:19:35,073
If you get the confession, I'll recommend
you to your preferred station.

269
00:19:36,241 --> 00:19:37,242
Huh?

270
00:19:39,711 --> 00:19:41,446
Do your best.

271
00:20:03,268 --> 00:20:04,403
Ms. Aya.

272
00:20:09,341 --> 00:20:10,709
What's wrong?

273
00:20:13,812 --> 00:20:15,480
-No--
-Sit down.

274
00:20:20,519 --> 00:20:24,957
They've already decided
I'm the culprit, haven't they?

275
00:20:25,924 --> 00:20:28,126
What did they tell you during questioning?

276
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:32,631
Who are those people?
They even brought up my debt.

277
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:38,136
What debt?

278
00:20:39,037 --> 00:20:42,941
My useless father's gambling debt.

279
00:20:44,109 --> 00:20:47,846
He tricked many people
and borrowed money everywhere.

280
00:20:49,014 --> 00:20:50,616
I'm paying it back.

281
00:20:51,183 --> 00:20:53,185
Did you explain that to the officers?

282
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:54,286
I did.

283
00:20:54,853 --> 00:20:56,121
I did, but…

284
00:20:56,188 --> 00:20:59,358
Do they even want to listen?

285
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:04,496
I hadn't seen my father in years.

286
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:08,834
I didn't even know
he got sleeping pills at the hospital.

287
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:11,703
As for Mr. Nikaido,

288
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:16,375
I don't even know who he is
or what he does.

289
00:21:16,908 --> 00:21:18,677
No matter how many times
I say I don't know,

290
00:21:18,744 --> 00:21:22,714
they say, "Think harder,"
or "A little digging will tell us."

291
00:21:25,517 --> 00:21:27,919
How can I make them believe me?

292
00:21:31,590 --> 00:21:35,661
Their job is to doubt suspects.

293
00:21:41,466 --> 00:21:44,770
If you say Mr. Nikaido was killed,

294
00:21:44,836 --> 00:21:48,907
I want you to find the culprit. That's why
I'm cooperating with the police.

295
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:51,743
Sorry for the trouble.

296
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:58,750
I never imagined
you would become a police officer.

297
00:22:00,485 --> 00:22:01,486
Well…

298
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,622
It just kind of happened.

299
00:22:05,390 --> 00:22:09,294
It's a job that helps
the world and people.

300
00:22:10,696 --> 00:22:13,231
It's not that great.

301
00:22:13,298 --> 00:22:15,500
It is! You're doing well.

302
00:22:23,141 --> 00:22:25,143
What do you really want to know?

303
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:30,015
The truth…

304
00:22:30,749 --> 00:22:33,418
about what happened on the mountain.

305
00:22:40,392 --> 00:22:45,931
Do you also think
I gave Mr. Nikaido the sleeping pill?

306
00:22:50,769 --> 00:22:52,170
Did you?

307
00:22:53,972 --> 00:22:55,073
What do you think?

308
00:23:04,082 --> 00:23:07,386
You don't know?
I guess you don't know me very well.

309
00:23:07,919 --> 00:23:10,822
Won't you tell me?

310
00:23:19,097 --> 00:23:20,098
I…

311
00:23:24,569 --> 00:23:25,937
I didn't do it.

312
00:23:26,671 --> 00:23:28,106
I didn't.

313
00:23:28,173 --> 00:23:29,908
The culprit is…

314
00:23:31,042 --> 00:23:32,544
someone else.

315
00:23:43,789 --> 00:23:45,323
-Hello.
-Hello.

316
00:23:45,390 --> 00:23:47,325
-Good work.
-Hello, sir.

317
00:23:47,392 --> 00:23:50,529
Do you think Saruwatari really did it?

318
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:55,066
As long as there's evidence,
we'll consider her a suspect.

319
00:23:57,569 --> 00:23:58,870
Mr. Endo.

320
00:24:28,266 --> 00:24:30,235
Hey! Ogoma, you're home.

321
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:31,870
Hello.

322
00:24:31,937 --> 00:24:33,104
Whoa!

323
00:24:34,072 --> 00:24:36,708
I made progress today!

324
00:24:36,775 --> 00:24:41,012
-I finally had a serious talk with Harune.
-I'm glad.

325
00:24:41,079 --> 00:24:43,582
From my position on the insurance side…

326
00:24:44,449 --> 00:24:45,717
Is your stomach hurting?

327
00:24:47,219 --> 00:24:48,653
Ogoma.

328
00:24:51,022 --> 00:24:52,958
Why are you coming in?

329
00:24:53,024 --> 00:24:54,926
I want to tell you a few things.

330
00:24:54,993 --> 00:24:56,061
Not today.

331
00:24:56,127 --> 00:24:57,195
That hurts.

332
00:24:58,263 --> 00:25:02,868
In my investigation,
Harune has no link to the others.

333
00:25:02,934 --> 00:25:06,304
The increase in the insurance
coverage has a reasonable cause.

334
00:25:06,938 --> 00:25:10,876
Since I can't find any evidence
that Harune, the beneficiary,

335
00:25:10,942 --> 00:25:15,080
was involved in Mr. Nikaido's death,
my insurance investigation must end.

336
00:25:16,014 --> 00:25:17,215
You're really ending it?

337
00:25:17,282 --> 00:25:21,753
Our time together was short,
but I learned a lot from you.

338
00:25:22,420 --> 00:25:25,624
We still don't know why Mr. Nikaido died!

339
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:29,794
Finding the culprit is a job
for you police, not me.

340
00:25:32,831 --> 00:25:35,333
But Ms. Tabatake is dead too.

341
00:25:38,703 --> 00:25:40,705
Wasn't it a suicide?

342
00:25:40,772 --> 00:25:41,940
It's under investigation.

343
00:25:44,075 --> 00:25:45,377
Let's eat.

344
00:25:49,481 --> 00:25:50,415
Let's eat.

345
00:25:54,386 --> 00:25:57,055
With the insurance Ms. Tabatake had

346
00:25:58,056 --> 00:26:00,992
if she died, 30 million yen
would go to Nono.

347
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:05,497
The contract was made two years ago.
If it's suicide, the money isn't paid.

348
00:26:06,831 --> 00:26:07,799
What?

349
00:26:09,134 --> 00:26:13,138
I mean, what if someone took out insurance
with the intention to kill themselves?

350
00:26:13,204 --> 00:26:15,407
They won't pay for a contract made
within two or three years.

351
00:26:16,942 --> 00:26:20,145
What happens to Nono then?

352
00:26:22,514 --> 00:26:23,548
Would Ms. Tabatake

353
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:28,320
really throw away 30 million yen
that she could give her daughter?

354
00:26:28,386 --> 00:26:31,590
-Money again--
-Nothing is more certain than money.

355
00:26:32,357 --> 00:26:36,194
So, for now,
this is the police's theory, right?

356
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:38,263
TOUR GUESTS

357
00:26:39,064 --> 00:26:45,303
Ms. Aya gave Mr. Nikaido
sleeping pills and killed him.

358
00:26:45,370 --> 00:26:46,871
Yes, that's about it.

359
00:26:47,505 --> 00:26:50,041
And your theory, Ogoma, is this.

360
00:26:50,108 --> 00:26:55,180
Ms. Tabatake
gave Mr. Nikaido the pills and killed him.

361
00:26:55,246 --> 00:26:59,784
Also, Ms. Tabatake was scared of someone.

362
00:26:59,851 --> 00:27:00,652
Who?

363
00:27:02,253 --> 00:27:03,088
Someone.

364
00:27:05,523 --> 00:27:06,625
Just "someone."

365
00:27:08,259 --> 00:27:10,729
"Someone."

366
00:27:11,529 --> 00:27:15,467
-Which one do you think it is?
-I don't care much anymore.

367
00:27:15,533 --> 00:27:17,268
You should care!

368
00:27:17,335 --> 00:27:19,671
Ms. Tabatake did many unnatural things.

369
00:27:19,738 --> 00:27:22,841
Like changing the beneficiary
on the hiking insurance.

370
00:27:22,907 --> 00:27:25,443
A mistake like that
would be a huge problem.

371
00:27:27,512 --> 00:27:28,546
Detective…

372
00:27:28,613 --> 00:27:29,681
She did say that.

373
00:27:29,748 --> 00:27:32,083
If she made a mistake
it would be a big problem.

374
00:27:33,084 --> 00:27:35,654
Something like that
could easily get her fired.

375
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:40,158
Changing it wouldn't get her the insurance
money either. So why take that risk?

376
00:27:40,225 --> 00:27:42,927
Would she take such a high risk?

377
00:27:42,994 --> 00:27:44,696
The fingerprints too.

378
00:27:44,763 --> 00:27:46,798
Ms. Tabatake's didn’t show up?

379
00:27:48,733 --> 00:27:50,168
If Ms. Aya were the culprit,

380
00:27:50,235 --> 00:27:53,038
I don't think she would be
so careless as to leave prints.

381
00:27:53,104 --> 00:27:56,074
Even discounting your bias for Ms. Aya,

382
00:27:56,141 --> 00:27:59,244
I agree that Ms. Tabatake's actions
look unnatural.

383
00:28:02,747 --> 00:28:06,718
If the three missing people were alive,

384
00:28:06,785 --> 00:28:10,321
we would know who is telling the truth.

385
00:28:13,658 --> 00:28:17,429
There's a record of a person
lost in the Andes

386
00:28:17,495 --> 00:28:20,298
who was rescued after 72 days.

387
00:28:21,332 --> 00:28:22,434
That long?

388
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:25,336
Mt. Shikara isn't as harsh as the Andes.

389
00:28:25,403 --> 00:28:28,440
If they're alive,
they would have come down by now.

390
00:28:31,543 --> 00:28:32,811
-Chief.
-Yeah?

391
00:28:33,378 --> 00:28:34,746
Can I be of help?

392
00:28:36,414 --> 00:28:37,816
If I can, please tell me.

393
00:28:37,882 --> 00:28:38,917
Yes.

394
00:28:54,999 --> 00:28:57,736
HQ wants to pin it on Saruwatari.

395
00:28:58,470 --> 00:29:00,071
Here, look at these too.

396
00:29:00,638 --> 00:29:03,908
I can't believe I got such a messy case
right before retirement.

397
00:29:03,975 --> 00:29:07,846
We're usually called for drunks fighting.

398
00:29:07,912 --> 00:29:09,814
-Right?
-Yes.

399
00:29:09,881 --> 00:29:11,649
Only small cases like those.

400
00:29:11,716 --> 00:29:13,084
True.

401
00:29:15,086 --> 00:29:19,390
I've been waiting for a big case too.

402
00:29:22,727 --> 00:29:24,195
Mr. Awashima,

403
00:29:26,397 --> 00:29:31,369
have you ever disagreed
with the higher-ups' plans?

404
00:29:33,571 --> 00:29:34,472
A few times.

405
00:29:35,740 --> 00:29:38,676
-Think they ever got a wrong lead?
-Yes.

406
00:29:40,478 --> 00:29:42,180
What did you do then?

407
00:29:46,985 --> 00:29:50,555
Followed the higher-ups' plan.
That's what officers do.

408
00:30:08,173 --> 00:30:09,174
Hello.

409
00:30:12,610 --> 00:30:13,611
Hello?

410
00:30:14,379 --> 00:30:16,414
-Can you hear me?
-I can.

411
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:20,018
Who is this?

412
00:30:20,084 --> 00:30:23,321
I'm Nono Tabatake.
I want to ask you something.

413
00:30:26,891 --> 00:30:29,928
-You… want to ask me?
-Yes.

414
00:30:39,604 --> 00:30:40,772
-Hello.
-Hello.

415
00:30:40,839 --> 00:30:42,807
-Please use the sanitizer.
-Okay.

416
00:30:44,976 --> 00:30:47,011
Brushing her teeth?

417
00:30:51,783 --> 00:30:55,086
I brought a get-well gift.
The doctor said it's okay.

418
00:30:59,824 --> 00:31:01,459
Here you go.

419
00:31:02,193 --> 00:31:06,397
Canned soup, warmed up.
It's hot, so be careful.

420
00:31:06,464 --> 00:31:07,932
Let's eat.

421
00:31:08,766 --> 00:31:11,236
Drinking this on a snowy mountain…

422
00:31:11,302 --> 00:31:13,771
It makes you feel alive.

423
00:31:19,744 --> 00:31:21,713
Better not talk about mountains.

424
00:31:29,320 --> 00:31:31,923
Okay, ask. I'm all ears.

425
00:31:32,991 --> 00:31:33,892
Okay.

426
00:31:34,459 --> 00:31:37,795
How much money does it take to live alone?

427
00:31:41,165 --> 00:31:43,801
You mean you, by yourself?

428
00:31:43,868 --> 00:31:47,138
When I leave the hospital, I want to go
back to the house where I lived with Mom.

429
00:31:55,246 --> 00:31:57,482
Is it impossible for me?

430
00:32:04,322 --> 00:32:05,356
Listen,

431
00:32:06,691 --> 00:32:07,859
Japan…

432
00:32:09,127 --> 00:32:13,698
has a rule that children in trouble
must not be left alone,

433
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:16,768
and adults must protect them.

434
00:32:16,834 --> 00:32:18,803
-A rule?
-Yes.

435
00:32:18,870 --> 00:32:21,139
It's called child welfare.

436
00:32:23,641 --> 00:32:27,145
My mom has life insurance, right?

437
00:32:27,211 --> 00:32:28,546
She does.

438
00:32:29,681 --> 00:32:33,618
My mom never gets involved
in dangerous trips.

439
00:32:33,685 --> 00:32:37,221
Dangerous trips make more money,

440
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:40,725
but she doesn't do them
because she always wants to come home.

441
00:32:44,963 --> 00:32:47,198
That’s a wonderful decision.

442
00:32:49,233 --> 00:32:51,502
"If Mommy is gone,

443
00:32:51,569 --> 00:32:54,339
I'll leave enough money
so you won't be in trouble.

444
00:32:54,405 --> 00:32:56,641
Don't worry." She told me so.

445
00:32:57,542 --> 00:33:00,678
Can I live alone on that money?

446
00:33:09,787 --> 00:33:10,922
Your mom

447
00:33:13,191 --> 00:33:15,360
really loved you.

448
00:33:27,505 --> 00:33:29,941
All of her life insurance money

449
00:33:31,476 --> 00:33:34,912
is proof of her love.

450
00:33:39,784 --> 00:33:44,689
Okay, I got it.
I'm now your personal advisor.

451
00:33:49,594 --> 00:33:51,829
If you have any questions, you can ask me.

452
00:33:55,733 --> 00:33:57,168
Was my Mommy…

453
00:33:59,137 --> 00:34:01,005
killed?

454
00:34:05,777 --> 00:34:07,278
Why do you think so?

455
00:34:09,914 --> 00:34:13,451
Was your mom being targeted
by someone scary?

456
00:34:18,289 --> 00:34:20,425
How old is Ms. Tabatake's daughter?

457
00:34:20,491 --> 00:34:23,127
She's eight, she's in third grade.

458
00:34:23,194 --> 00:34:25,630
Any relatives to take her in?

459
00:34:25,696 --> 00:34:28,166
There are, but it looks tough.

460
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:31,069
So she'll go to an orphanage.

461
00:34:31,135 --> 00:34:36,007
She says she wants
to live alone in her old home.

462
00:34:39,577 --> 00:34:43,314
Nao, if an eight-year-old girl

463
00:34:43,381 --> 00:34:47,785
said she wanted to live alone,
would you say "go ahead"?

464
00:34:47,852 --> 00:34:52,190
No way. I wouldn’t allow
something that dangerous.

465
00:34:52,256 --> 00:34:56,094
Yes. She still needs
someone to care for her.

466
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:12,810
I can't object to that.

467
00:35:14,378 --> 00:35:15,646
But is there a way to--

468
00:35:15,713 --> 00:35:19,550
Is this relevant? You're being distracted.

469
00:35:19,617 --> 00:35:23,888
I'm not. I'm heading to Harune's place.

470
00:35:23,955 --> 00:35:26,290
To see her financial records.

471
00:35:41,606 --> 00:35:43,107
Can I get another speeding ticket?

472
00:35:43,174 --> 00:35:45,243
You know I would never say yes.

473
00:35:45,309 --> 00:35:48,946
Wait, Harune! Wait!

474
00:35:49,013 --> 00:35:50,515
Wait!

475
00:35:51,516 --> 00:35:53,251
How is it? Will you be done today?

476
00:35:53,885 --> 00:35:56,154
Ogoma, you can return
to normal duty after tomorrow.

477
00:35:56,220 --> 00:35:58,789
-Why?
-Because we want you to.

478
00:35:58,856 --> 00:36:00,725
Is it because I know the suspect?

479
00:36:00,791 --> 00:36:02,894
I already told you.
She's an old acquaintance!

480
00:36:02,960 --> 00:36:04,462
It's a decided matter.

481
00:36:04,529 --> 00:36:07,798
I have to ask Harune why Ms. Tabatake
called Nikaido "Tsugaru".

482
00:36:07,865 --> 00:36:09,433
-Please. Take care.
-Chief.

483
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:10,701
Bye!

484
00:36:10,768 --> 00:36:12,236
-Bye.
-Chief.

485
00:36:13,337 --> 00:36:15,673
-You want to be promoted, don't you?
-Yes.

486
00:36:15,740 --> 00:36:17,675
This time, stay out of it.

487
00:36:18,576 --> 00:36:19,877
Don't get involved.

488
00:36:22,013 --> 00:36:25,683
Mr. Awashima, you think
something is off too, don't you?

489
00:36:25,750 --> 00:36:28,853
Tabatake, the center of the case,
suddenly died,

490
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:31,022
and the next day,
it was already judged a suicide.

491
00:36:31,088 --> 00:36:32,890
Even though there's no suicide note.

492
00:36:33,457 --> 00:36:37,094
No information about Nikaido's wife
or the other tour guests

493
00:36:37,161 --> 00:36:39,297
has been provided by the higher-ups.

494
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:43,100
Are the higher-ups hiding something?

495
00:36:43,167 --> 00:36:46,938
They say the search
for the missing might end tomorrow.

496
00:36:47,004 --> 00:36:48,339
They're ending it?

497
00:36:48,406 --> 00:36:50,208
Enough. Don't get involved.

498
00:36:51,409 --> 00:36:52,577
Trust me on this.

499
00:36:53,144 --> 00:36:55,346
Mr. Awashima and Masaru.

500
00:36:55,413 --> 00:36:57,014
-Yes.
-The two of you…

501
00:36:57,982 --> 00:36:59,584
It's over!

502
00:36:59,650 --> 00:37:00,851
I was so stupid!

503
00:37:01,652 --> 00:37:02,820
Tsugaru?

504
00:37:02,887 --> 00:37:04,255
She called him that.

505
00:37:04,322 --> 00:37:05,256
150 MILLION YEN

506
00:37:10,261 --> 00:37:12,096
Doubt everything.

507
00:37:13,064 --> 00:37:17,101
Once you have doubted everything,
what remains is the truth.

508
00:37:18,569 --> 00:37:20,238
Call me.

509
00:37:20,304 --> 00:37:22,473
-On my phone.
-I'm leaving first.

510
00:37:27,411 --> 00:37:28,646
What is it?

511
00:37:28,713 --> 00:37:29,847
Harune got away!

512
00:37:29,914 --> 00:37:30,982
What?

513
00:37:31,048 --> 00:37:33,951
I was fooled. I was stupid to trust her.

514
00:37:34,018 --> 00:37:36,053
What are you talking about?
Where did she go?

515
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:37,054
Probably Tokyo.

516
00:37:37,121 --> 00:37:39,056
-Why Tokyo?
-I knew it.

517
00:37:39,123 --> 00:37:40,725
That woman is suspicious.

518
00:37:41,425 --> 00:37:44,195
Who benefits when Mr. Nikaido dies?

519
00:37:44,762 --> 00:37:46,797
Harune, of course.

520
00:37:46,864 --> 00:37:49,200
She ran because she knows something?

521
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:51,068
-I'll find her and make her confess.
-No.

522
00:37:51,135 --> 00:37:53,671
-What?
-Us police will catch her first.

523
00:37:56,474 --> 00:37:58,042
-I'll be first.
-No!

524
00:37:58,109 --> 00:38:00,211
I'll find her
and make her talk right away.

525
00:38:00,278 --> 00:38:02,079
Tell me the details.

526
00:38:02,980 --> 00:38:04,482
-Ogoma!
-Yes?

527
00:38:04,548 --> 00:38:06,217
Want to go for a drink?

528
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:09,920
I'm going home. I'm taking leave tomorrow.

529
00:38:10,421 --> 00:38:12,123
Okay! I'm off!

530
00:38:13,858 --> 00:38:16,727
You don’t need to take leave for this.

531
00:38:24,735 --> 00:38:26,103
It's Ogoma.

532
00:38:27,171 --> 00:38:29,073
Don't admit to what you didn't do.

533
00:38:36,147 --> 00:38:38,983
WE WON'T BE ABLE TO MEET FOR A WHILE
HANG ON UNTIL I GET BACK

534
00:38:59,704 --> 00:39:01,238
Thank you for waiting.

535
00:39:01,305 --> 00:39:06,143
Japan Airlines to Tokyo Haneda,
departing at 9:50 a.m.

536
00:39:06,210 --> 00:39:07,978
Wait for me. I'll catch you, Harune.

537
00:39:08,546 --> 00:39:10,181
-So cool.
-Are you making fun of me?

538
00:39:10,247 --> 00:39:12,116
-I am.
-Huh?

539
00:39:12,183 --> 00:39:13,951
-Just kidding.
-Try again, please.

540
00:39:14,018 --> 00:39:14,852
Here.

541
00:39:14,919 --> 00:39:15,920
Try again.

542
00:39:15,986 --> 00:39:17,421
-What are you doing?
-I'm…

543
00:39:25,129 --> 00:39:28,099
-Gather all the CCTV data you can.
-Yes.

544
00:39:28,165 --> 00:39:31,001
-If they refuse, persuade them.
-We've arrived!

545
00:39:31,068 --> 00:39:32,470
This way.

546
00:39:32,536 --> 00:39:35,506
Ogoma, this way.

547
00:39:36,507 --> 00:39:38,509
Do we have anything to cool him down?

548
00:39:38,576 --> 00:39:39,577
I'll go look.

549
00:39:39,643 --> 00:39:41,579
-Nao!
-How are you doing?

550
00:39:41,645 --> 00:39:42,947
Who is that?

551
00:39:43,013 --> 00:39:45,549
-A detective from Hokkaido.
-Who hurt him?

552
00:39:46,117 --> 00:39:47,518
No one.

553
00:39:52,089 --> 00:39:52,923
Huh?

554
00:39:53,491 --> 00:39:54,625
Mr. Nao?

555
00:39:54,692 --> 00:39:56,026
Where are you, Ogoma?

556
00:39:56,093 --> 00:39:57,928
In front of the station.

557
00:39:57,995 --> 00:39:59,630
What do you see?

558
00:39:59,697 --> 00:40:01,565
Lots of people.

559
00:40:01,632 --> 00:40:02,566
There you are.

560
00:40:02,633 --> 00:40:04,702
Where were you going?

561
00:40:09,473 --> 00:40:10,975
Wow!

562
00:40:18,649 --> 00:40:19,950
First time in Tokyo?

563
00:40:20,985 --> 00:40:24,121
Yes. It's so humid!

564
00:40:24,188 --> 00:40:29,126
He's worn out by the crowds.
His place in Hokkaido is really remote.

565
00:40:29,193 --> 00:40:30,594
Don’t push yourself. Rest.

566
00:40:30,661 --> 00:40:31,695
No, I'm fine.

567
00:40:32,396 --> 00:40:34,865
-Any idea where Harune went?
-Yes.

568
00:40:34,932 --> 00:40:37,301
Nikaido owns a condo in Shibuya.

569
00:40:37,368 --> 00:40:38,202
Shibuya?

570
00:40:38,269 --> 00:40:39,804
-I gotta go--
-Rest!

571
00:40:39,870 --> 00:40:40,971
Okay.

572
00:40:41,038 --> 00:40:45,376
I'll send you security camera footage
from around the condo. Check all of it.

573
00:40:46,076 --> 00:40:47,111
I have to do it?

574
00:40:47,178 --> 00:40:49,580
Of course. Hurry up.

575
00:40:49,647 --> 00:40:51,115
Find Harune already.

576
00:40:51,182 --> 00:40:55,186
I don't want to pay 150 million yen
to that shady woman!

577
00:40:57,955 --> 00:41:00,357
How many hours of footage are there?

578
00:41:01,091 --> 00:41:02,326
Don't force yourself.

579
00:41:02,393 --> 00:41:04,995
No, I'm okay.

580
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:07,598
All right.

581
00:41:08,466 --> 00:41:11,802
How is Ms. Aya doing?

582
00:41:11,869 --> 00:41:14,171
The police interrogate her every day.

583
00:41:14,238 --> 00:41:15,573
Figures.

584
00:41:15,639 --> 00:41:17,541
I don't know anything anymore.

585
00:41:18,242 --> 00:41:21,745
About what's true and who's lying.

586
00:41:21,812 --> 00:41:25,816
Honestly, I only learned about
murder cases at the police academy.

587
00:41:28,152 --> 00:41:31,822
I lost Harune
because I couldn't doubt her.

588
00:41:31,889 --> 00:41:35,359
I should've doubted her
before trusting her.

589
00:41:35,426 --> 00:41:37,261
Doubt everything.

590
00:41:37,328 --> 00:41:38,629
Exactly.

591
00:41:42,766 --> 00:41:44,268
Ogoma.

592
00:41:44,335 --> 00:41:47,571
-Yes?
-Right now, who do you doubt the most?

593
00:41:50,441 --> 00:41:51,542
The police.

594
00:41:55,646 --> 00:41:57,748
You shouldn't say that
as a police officer.

595
00:41:59,683 --> 00:42:02,686
You overturned
police investigations before, right?

596
00:42:03,420 --> 00:42:05,656
Yeah. The Hakodate case?

597
00:42:05,723 --> 00:42:07,324
Or the Sapporo one?

598
00:42:11,428 --> 00:42:13,130
The investigation was sloppy.

599
00:42:14,198 --> 00:42:16,333
The higher-ups wanted
to hide their mistake

600
00:42:16,400 --> 00:42:18,435
and bent the facts to do it.

601
00:42:18,936 --> 00:42:23,274
That was a long time ago.

602
00:42:27,211 --> 00:42:29,313
May I tell an old story too?

603
00:42:31,282 --> 00:42:33,117
-Sure.
-Here goes.

604
00:42:35,185 --> 00:42:38,923
In my hometown, innocent people
were often arrested.

605
00:42:38,989 --> 00:42:41,559
Your hometown had no laws or justice.

606
00:42:42,793 --> 00:42:46,697
I thought the police were trash,
so I joined the police.

607
00:42:47,831 --> 00:42:50,334
That's a rare reason to join.

608
00:42:51,669 --> 00:42:56,707
I figured if I joined the police,
I could make the world more peaceful.

609
00:42:58,275 --> 00:43:00,277
And then? What happened?

610
00:43:06,617 --> 00:43:07,585
Ogoma?

611
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:10,254
Harune?

612
00:43:11,522 --> 00:43:13,223
Not her. That's a man.

613
00:43:14,625 --> 00:43:15,626
Who?

614
00:43:16,594 --> 00:43:18,128
Is that Mr. Monden?

615
00:43:18,195 --> 00:43:19,964
-Ryutaro Monden?
-Yes.

616
00:43:20,030 --> 00:43:22,866
-The missing guy? Wait!
-Yes.

617
00:43:22,933 --> 00:43:24,969
Is it him? Or someone who looks like him?

618
00:43:25,035 --> 00:43:27,404
-Why?
-Be quiet! Give me a moment!

619
00:43:28,038 --> 00:43:29,006
Here.

620
00:43:33,344 --> 00:43:34,445
Look!

621
00:43:35,679 --> 00:43:36,880
It's Mr. Monden, right?

622
00:43:45,089 --> 00:43:48,626
JULY 27, 2:00 P.M.

623
00:43:50,761 --> 00:43:54,965
He's supposed to be missing,
so why is he in Shibuya?

624
00:43:56,800 --> 00:43:58,268
He's alive.

625
00:44:00,437 --> 00:44:01,672
He's a witness.

626
00:44:04,508 --> 00:44:06,677
He's pretending to be missing?

627
00:44:06,744 --> 00:44:08,879
So we'll investigate
and not tell the police?

628
00:44:08,946 --> 00:44:10,714
What is this?

629
00:44:10,781 --> 00:44:13,150
Make sure you come back.
Saruwatari is about to confess…

630
00:44:13,217 --> 00:44:14,184
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
